.\n\nThe next steps in the infant's care should include:\n\n* Continued monitoring of the infant's respiratory status and oxygenation\n* Further evaluation of the infant's cardiac and pulmonary function using echocardiography and other imaging studies\n* Consideration of other treatments for PPHN, such as extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (ECMO) or high-frequency ventilation\n* Evaluation of the infant's long-term prognosis and potential for developmental delays or other long-term complications.\n\nIn terms of potential complications, PPHN can lead to respiratory failure, cardiac arrest, and other serious complications. The use of inhaled nitric oxide can help to reduce the risk of these complications, but close monitoring and prompt intervention are necessary to prevent or manage them.\n\nThe long-term prognosis for infants with PPHN is variable and depends on the underlying cause and severity of the condition. Some infants may experience developmental delays or other long-term complications, while others may recover fully. A comprehensive evaluation and management plan is necessary to optimize the infant's outcome. \n", "vote_history": [{"**\n\nThe newborn boy is experiencing tachypnea (rapid breathing rate) and increased work of breathing": "yes", "Carefully read the medical scenario presented in the question**\n\nThe newborn boy is experiencing tachypnea (rapid breathing) and has elevated pulmonary artery pressure.": "no"}, {"**\n\nThe newborn boy is experiencing tachypnea (rapid breathing rate) and increased work of breathing": "yes", "Carefully read the medical scenario presented in the question**\n\nThe newborn boy is experiencing tachypnea (rapid breathing) and has elevated pulmonary artery pressure.": "yes"}], "revision_history": [{"Carefully read the medical scenario presented in the question**\n\nThe newborn boy is experiencing tachypnea (rapid breathing) and has elevated pulmonary artery pressure.": "Revisions: \nThe provided medical report is a good s